[32m+[m[32m# TapLog Constitution[m
 [m
 ## Core Principles[m
 [m
[31m-### [PRINCIPLE_1_NAME][m
[31m-<!-- Example: I. Library-First -->[m
[31m-[PRINCIPLE_1_DESCRIPTION][m
[31m-<!-- Example: Every feature starts as a standalone library; Libraries must be self-contained, independently testable, documented; Clear purpose required - no organizational-only libraries -->[m
[32m+[m[32m### I. Event-First, Channel-Independent Core[m
[32m+[m[32mTapLog's fundamental product primitive is **EVENT + TIMESTAMP**. App, Widget,[m
[32m+[m[32mQuick Settings, NFC, and Natural Language are input channels to one Event system,[m
[32m+[m[32mnot separate Event systems or products. The Event Engine MUST remain independent[m
[32m+[m[32mof channel-specific UI, platform dispatch, and interaction behavior so that a valid[m
[32m+[m[32mEvent request has the same domain meaning regardless of its origin.[m
 [m
[31m-### [PRINCIPLE_2_NAME][m
[31m-<!-- Example: II. CLI Interface -->[m
[31m-[PRINCIPLE_2_DESCRIPTION][m
[31m-<!-- Example: Every library exposes functionality via CLI; Text in/out protocol: stdin/args → stdout, errors → stderr; Support JSON + human-readable formats -->[m
[32m+[m[32mRationale: a unified, channel-independent core preserves consistent history and[m
[32m+[m[32mallows channels to evolve without redefining the product's data semantics.[m
 [m
[31m-### [PRINCIPLE_3_NAME][m
[31m-<!-- Example: III. Test-First (NON-NEGOTIABLE) -->[m
[31m-[PRINCIPLE_3_DESCRIPTION][m
[31m-<!-- Example: TDD mandatory: Tests written → User approved → Tests fail → Then implement; Red-Green-Refactor cycle strictly enforced -->[m
[32m+[m[32m### II. Local-First Core and Optional Intelligence[m
[32m+[m[32mV1 is Android-only and MUST provide core Event logging without an account or an[m
[32m+[m[32minternet connection. Deterministic, local parsing MUST support the Natural Language[m
[32m+[m[32minput path when AI is unavailable. AI MAY enhance supported devices, but MUST NOT be[m
[32m+[m[32mrequired to create, interpret, or retain core Events.[m
 [m
[31m-### [PRINCIPLE_4_NAME][m
[31m-<!-- Example: IV. Integration Testing -->[m
[31m-[PRINCIPLE_4_DESCRIPTION][m
[31m-<!-- Example: Focus areas requiring integration tests: New library contract tests, Contract changes, Inter-service communication, Shared schemas -->[m
[32m+[m[32mRationale: personal logging must remain available, private by default, and reliable[m
[32m+[m[32munder ordinary offline conditions.[m
 [m
[31m-### [PRINCIPLE_5_NAME][m
[31m-<!-- Example: V. Observability, VI. Versioning & Breaking Changes, VII. Simplicity -->[m
