[32m+[m[32m### III. Preserve History and Confirm Ambiguity[m
[32m+[m[32mHistory is sacred: Events and their historical meaning MUST be preserved through[m
[32m+[m[32mordinary edits, corrections, archive operations, and lifecycle changes. Data may be[m
[32m+[m[32mpermanently removed only after the user explicitly chooses a clearly communicated,[m
[32m+[m[32mirreversible permanent-deletion action. When user intent, matching, or action is[m
[32m+[m[32mambiguous, the system MUST obtain the minimum necessary confirmation rather than[m
[32m+[m[32msilently mutating data or guessing incorrectly.[m
 [m
[31m-## [SECTION_2_NAME][m
[31m-<!-- Example: Additional Constraints, Security Requirements, Performance Standards, etc. -->[m
[32m+[m[32mRationale: TapLog is a record of real events; trust depends on accurate intent and[m
[32m+[m[32mthe user's control over irreversible loss.[m
 [m
[31m-[SECTION_2_CONTENT][m
