[32m+[m[32m### IV. Channel-Owned Interaction Safety[m
[32m+[m[32mDuplicate suppression and interaction handling MUST be implemented by the individual[m
[32m+[m[32minput/channel layer. The Event Engine MUST NOT apply a global debounce that rejects[m
[32m+[m[32ma valid Event request. Channel behavior MUST preserve intentional consecutive user[m
[32m+[m[32mactions, including repeated Counter increments.[m
 [m
[31m-## [SECTION_3_NAME][m
[31m-<!-- Example: Development Workflow, Review Process, Quality Gates, etc. -->[m
[32m+[m[32mRationale: physical NFC reads, widget interactions, tiles, and in-app actions have[m
[32m+[m[32mdifferent failure and feedback characteristics; global suppression would corrupt[m
[32m+[m[32mlegitimate event history.[m
 [m
[31m-[SECTION_3_CONTENT][m
[31m-<!-- Example: Code review requirements, testing gates, deployment approval process, etc. -->[m
[32m+[m[32m### V. Testable Boundaries and Scope Discipline[m
[32m+[m[32mDomain and application behavior MUST be independently testable from Android UI and[m
[32m+[m[32mframework code. Changes to domain or application behavior MUST follow test-driven[m
[32m+[m[32mdevelopment. Modules and interfaces MUST have clear responsibilities; channel and[m
[32m+[m[32mAndroid integration code MUST not absorb Event Engine semantics. V1 MUST NOT include[m
[32m+[m[32mFuture Scope items unless the PRD is explicitly amended to promote them.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mRationale: explicit boundaries protect product semantics, enable reliable tests, and[m
[32m+[m[32mkeep the first release focused.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Product and Platform Constraints[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAll implementation work MUST be traceable to the current[m
[32m+[m[32m`docs/product/TapLog_V1_PRD.md`; the PRD is authoritative for product behavior.[m
[32m+[m[32mTechnical TBDs in that PRD remain undecided and MUST NOT be converted into[m
[32m+[m[32marchitecture, persistence, encryption, parser, lifecycle, or UI commitments without[m
[32m+[m[32man approved feature design.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mProduct and onboarding copy MUST make honest, platform-aware claims. In particular,[m
[32m+[m[32mcopy MUST NOT promise unconditional NFC behavior across locked screens, Android[m
[32m+[m[32mversions, devices, or OEM implementations. It may describe the intended interaction[m
[32m+[m[32mwithout implying guarantees Android or OEM behavior cannot provide.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Development Workflow[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWork feature-by-feature and one independently verifiable implementation task at a[m
[32m+[m[32mtime. Use Spec Kit artifacts as the canonical feature specification, plan, and task[m
[32m+[m[32msources; do not create competing artifacts. Each implemented feature requires an[m
[32m+[m[32mapproved specification traceable to the PRD; a product behavior change requires an[m
[32m+[m[32mapproved PRD amendment before implementation.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBefore implementation, identify the applicable principle and PRD requirement. Tests[m
[32m+[m[32mfor domain/application behavior are written first, observed to fail for the intended[m
[32m+[m[32mreason, then implemented and refactored. Completion claims require proportionate,[m
[32m+[m[32mexecuted verification and review of constitutional compliance, including local-first[m
[32m+[m[32moperation, history preservation, ambiguity handling, and channel independence where[m
[32m+[m[32mapplicable.[m
