[32m+[m[32mThis constitution governs project-wide engineering and product constraints. It does[m
[32m+[m[32mnot replace the PRD, which defines feature behavior, nor does it decide PRD Technical[m
[32m+[m[32mTBDs. In a conflict, the PRD governs product behavior; this constitution governs how[m
[32m+[m[32mthat behavior is designed and implemented without expanding V1 scope.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAmendments MUST document the reason, affected principles or sections, and any needed[m
[32m+[m[32mupdates to dependent Spec Kit artifacts. Constitutional compliance MUST be reviewed[m
[32m+[m[32mfor every feature specification, plan, task set, implementation review, and release[m
[32m+[m[32mverification. A change that introduces a new principle or materially expands a rule[m
[32m+[m[32mincrements the MINOR version; a backward-incompatible removal or redefinition[m
[32m+[m[32mincrements MAJOR; clarifications and non-semantic wording changes increment PATCH.[m
